        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): cap trigger script tool access",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where a restricted agent could create a recurring cron job with a trigger script and a `systemEvent` payload, then have that script receive the full coding tool surface. Main-session cron jobs require `systemEvent`, so the common path bypassed the creator's tool policy whenever cron triggers were enabled.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe creator tool cap now applies whenever a cron job has a trigger script, in addition to isolated `agentTurn` jobs. The cap is retained on every cron payload shape, survives updates, is persisted through the cron SQLite store so it survives a gateway restart, and is passed to the headless trigger evaluator. This keeps the existing agent-turn behavior while covering main-session system events and command payloads.\n\nDistinct from #12736, which concerns global cron deny policy; #97317 and #101349, which concern isolated agent-turn defaults; and #41484, which concerns elevated execution scope.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents restricted to a small tool set can use cron triggers without acquiring shell, exec, or patch capabilities beyond that set. Existing unrestricted operator-created cron jobs continue to work with their configured policy.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts src/agents/tools/cron-tool.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` passed: 144 checks.\n- `node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.cron.config.ts src/cron/normalize.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` passed: 59 checks.\n- `node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.cron.config.ts src/cron/service.jobs.test.ts src/cron/trigger-script.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` passed: 92 checks.\n- `node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway-client.config.ts packages/gateway-protocol/src/cron-validators.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` passed: 23 checks.\n- `src/cron/store.test.ts` restart-aware round-trip coverage added for the `systemEvent` and `command` tool caps; both fail on the pre-persistence codec and pass here.\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs` on the changed files, `oxfmt --check` on the changed files, and the core `run-tsgo.mjs` lane completed cleanly.\n- Restart cap-loss and reload proof, pinned to the current head, is in the re-review comment: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/104430#issuecomment-4945702410\n- Blacksmith Testbox could not start because its client is unavailable, and direct Crabbox is not configured. Broad remote validation was therefore not run.\n\n## Real behavior proof\nBehavior addressed: A cron trigger script created by a restricted caller must not receive tools the caller cannot use; a `systemEvent` main-session job with a trigger script previously kept no tool cap.\nReal environment tested: The production `createCronTool` entry point (`src/agents/tools/cron-tool.ts`) driven via `tool.execute(\"add\", ...)` on pristine main `d5fe0c5e73` and on PR head `711292119844c93e432a3b39b8897f31dbf92750` with the identical restricted creator (`creatorToolAllowlist: [\"read\", \"cron\"]`) creating a trigger-script `systemEvent` job; only the gateway RPC boundary was replaced to capture the params the tool sends.\nExact steps or command run after this patch: `PROOF_OUT=/tmp/proof-after.txt node_modules/.bin/tsx cron-trigger-proof.ts` (harness invokes the real cron tool `add` with `trigger.script` + `payload.kind=systemEvent`, prints the captured `cron.add` payload)\nEvidence after fix:\n```\n# BEFORE (pristine main d5fe0c5e73, identical restricted-caller input)\n{\"kind\":\"systemEvent\",\"text\":\"changed\"}\n# AFTER (this patch, head 711292119844c93e432a3b39b8897f31dbf92750, identical input)\n{\"kind\":\"systemEvent\",\"text\":\"changed\",\"toolsAllow\":[\"read\",\"cron\"]}\n```\nObserved result after fix: The persisted trigger-script job carries `toolsAllow: [\"read\",\"cron\"]`, capping the trigger to exactly the creator-visible tools instead of receiving the full coding tool surface.\nWhat was not tested: No live gateway tick with a provider-backed trigger evaluation, and the full build was not run.\n\n",
        "branch": "fix/cron-trigger-script-tools-cap",
